---
name: all_finite
---

# all_finite

Whether every cell of a list is finite (`finite`). The empty list is
vacuously all-finite. This is the domain guard the statistics
functions' specs use: infinities break bounds clauses (the mean of
`-Inf` and `+Inf` is `NaN`, which sorts after `+Inf` in the total
order, design §3.7).

```soil-sig
all_finite : (xs : List F64) -> Bool
```

```test classifies
([]) => true
([1.0, -0.0, 2.5]) => true
([1.0, "NaN", 2.5]) => false
(["-Inf"]) => false
```
